Chengyin IM — development preview
==============================

This package installs only the Fcitx 5 module, its two registration files and
documentation. It does not change the active input method, restart Fcitx, edit
environment variables or install files into a user's home directory.

After installation, restart Fcitx using your desktop's normal service controls.
In the Fcitx configuration tool, add "Chengyin 全拼（原型）". Its configuration accepts
an absolute UTF-8 TSV dictionary path. An empty path selects the 98-entry demo.
The file is a replacement vocabulary, not an overlay on the demo vocabulary.

TSV columns: apostrophe-separated lowercase pinyin, text, positive frequency.
Use literal TAB separators. Example: ni'hao<TAB>你好<TAB>3000
Limits: 64 MiB source, 250,000 entries, 63 pinyin bytes, 256 text bytes per entry.
Loading and old-dictionary reclamation run in a worker. A failed load keeps the
current vocabulary and is not saved over the working configuration. Compositions
already in progress finish with the old vocabulary before switching.

Settings are saved in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fcitx5/conf/chengyin.conf (normally
~/.config/fcitx5/conf/chengyin.conf), with a top-level DictionaryPath=/absolute/path.
After manually changing this file or replacing a TSV at the same path, use
fcitx5-remote -r to reload configuration. There is no file watcher.

Remove the input method from Fcitx's configuration list, then remove this package
with your package manager. User settings and custom vocabularies are preserved.

This is a test package built for its build distribution/architecture. Dependency
minimum versions are extracted from the linked libraries; it is not a portable
binary for all Debian/Ubuntu releases. No maintainer scripts are installed.
Desktop X11/Wayland validation and production vocabulary/whole-sentence decoding
are still pending. Keep an existing input method available during testing.

Project: https://github.com/zzttzzmyswy/myswyIm
